{"id":56034,"ord":134,"n_segments":180,"prev":56033,"next":56035,"doc":{"id":"68098","title":"68098_Snub Mosley oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Snub Mosley","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68098/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68098"},"chapter":"Queens Terrace, Decca records and Amen","title":"Photographs, vocalist Gordon Magey and sweet singing","category":"person_portrait","summary":"A blind singer who sang Blue Memories beautifully, shown in photos.","period":"1940","year_from":1940,"year_to":1940,"words":139,"start":[213,3],"end":[214,11],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68098#s56034","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[{"name":"Queens Terrace","focus":0,"city":"Woodside"}],"bands":[{"name":"Snub Mosley's band","focus":1,"leader":"Snub Mosley"}]},"people":[{"name":"Gordon Magey","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Willard Brown","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Bob Carroll","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Lloyd Phillips","qid":"Q41798556","n":1},{"name":"Vernon King","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":15,"theme_name":"Singers and the musicians who accompanied them","community":28,"community_name":"Band singers and accompanying vocalists","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":213,"b":3,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Would you want some pictures of the different bands?"},{"p":213,"b":4,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Yeah."},{"p":213,"b":5,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"I've got pictures of every band."},{"p":213,"b":6,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Why don't we look at them now, we can comment on those on the tape."},{"p":213,"b":7,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Where were we?"},{"p":213,"b":8,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"We were looking at this. These were made in March of '40, when you were at the Queens Terrace. Bob Carroll, Willard Brown, Lloyd Phillips, Vernon King--who is this guy, Gordon Magey."},{"p":213,"b":9,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Gordon Magey, he's the"},{"p":214,"b":0,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"He's blind?"},{"p":214,"b":1,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Yeah."},{"p":214,"b":2,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"\"I'm Just a Substitute for Love\"; he wasn't working with the band; was he?"},{"p":214,"b":3,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"He was my vocalist; yeah."},{"p":214,"b":4,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"This was the kind of number he was doing?"},{"p":214,"b":5,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"He was a sweet singer. He did a really beautiful job on \"Blue Memories.\""},{"p":214,"b":6,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Whatever happend to him?"},{"p":214,"b":7,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"He was listening the other day."},{"p":214,"b":8,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"He's still alive?"},{"p":214,"b":9,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"Yeah."},{"p":214,"b":10,"s":"MR. DRIGGS","x":"Where is he from, around here?"},{"p":214,"b":11,"s":"MR. MOSLEY","x":"He's from around here."}]}